WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.968 --> 00:00:02.000
-I'm so happy you're here.

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:03.334
Thank you for
coming back on the show.

00:00:03.334 --> 00:00:05.167
-I'm happy to be here.
-Happy to have you in person.

00:00:05.167 --> 00:00:07.234
Last time you were on,
we were Zooming.

00:00:07.234 --> 00:00:08.934
-Oh, my God.
-Remember that?

00:00:08.934 --> 00:00:10.467
-Oh, yeah.
-Remember the Zoom days?

00:00:10.467 --> 00:00:12.067
-And I was trying to
quiet my dog

00:00:12.067 --> 00:00:13.767
in the back and do everything.

00:00:13.767 --> 00:00:15.834
-By the way, the puppy --
I wanted to talk about this,

00:00:15.834 --> 00:00:17.067
'cause this is your puppy.

00:00:17.067 --> 00:00:19.400
You just got this during the --
Look at how cute.

00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:22.767
Bailey.
-That was a pandemic dog.

00:00:22.767 --> 00:00:24.000
-I mean, come on.
Which one is the stuffed animal?

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:26.934
-And now he's grown.
-Yeah. And then look.

00:00:26.934 --> 00:00:29.000
Bailey grown up. Look.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:31.434
Wow.
[ Audience "Awws" ]

00:00:31.434 --> 00:00:33.400
And how is puppy?

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:35.968
-Bailey has taken over.
-Just has, right?

00:00:35.968 --> 00:00:37.334
-Bailey's taken over
the whole house.

00:00:37.334 --> 00:00:38.567
He knows how to open doors.

00:00:38.567 --> 00:00:42.133
He knows how to go to the pantry
to sneak snacks.

00:00:42.133 --> 00:00:43.934
And then Bailey --
We got him dog food.

00:00:43.934 --> 00:00:47.334
He was like,
"I don't want that [bleep]

00:00:47.334 --> 00:00:49.033
-He grew up fast.

00:00:49.033 --> 00:00:52.267
-"Y'all have an organic diet.
I want organic food, too."

00:00:52.267 --> 00:00:54.167
Now we have Farmer's Dog.
-Oh, my God.

00:00:54.167 --> 00:00:57.400
-We got it on rotation.
-Gourmet dog now.

00:00:57.400 --> 00:00:59.467
-Bailey goes to the vet.
-Oh, my God.

00:00:59.467 --> 00:01:00.934
Bailey drives himself?

00:01:00.934 --> 00:01:03.234
-No, we drive him,
but at this point,

00:01:03.234 --> 00:01:06.000
I'm looking at those vet bills
and I'm like,

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:10.200
"When I had a dog when I was a
kid, our dog ate Alpo."

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:12.601
-Yeah, of course.
-If that.

00:01:12.601 --> 00:01:14.033
There was sometimes when
I was like,

00:01:14.033 --> 00:01:15.601
"I don't know
what the hell my dog ate."

00:01:15.601 --> 00:01:17.801
-Yeah, now the dog
has Uber Eats.

00:01:17.801 --> 00:01:19.534
-Yeah, exactly.

00:01:19.534 --> 00:01:22.267
-I was giving your intro,
and just what a great intro.

00:01:22.267 --> 00:01:26.234
I mean, you've won an Oscar,
an Emmy, a Golden Globe, a Tony.

00:01:26.234 --> 00:01:28.467
You've won everything.
I mean, well deserved.

00:01:28.467 --> 00:01:30.501
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:30.501 --> 00:01:32.267
Giant movie this weekend.

00:01:32.267 --> 00:01:34.534
But you're also a number-1

00:01:34.534 --> 00:01:36.200
"New York Times"
best-selling author.

00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:38.000
Congratulations to Viola Davis.

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:40.534
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:01:40.534 --> 00:01:41.901
-You know what?

00:01:41.901 --> 00:01:44.701
The only thing I could think
about with this book is,

00:01:44.701 --> 00:01:49.267
my daughter's always saying,
"Mom, you've got a god complex."

00:01:49.267 --> 00:01:52.133
So, I can't --
But I'm very proud of the book.

00:01:52.133 --> 00:01:53.667
That's all
I'm going to say, Genesis.

00:01:53.667 --> 00:01:55.667
-Yes.

00:01:55.667 --> 00:01:59.067
I love that this has been
number 1 for weeks now,

00:01:59.067 --> 00:02:00.400
"New York Times" best seller.

00:02:00.400 --> 00:02:02.667
-Yes.
-Is it hard to write a memoir?

00:02:02.667 --> 00:02:05.033
Is it therapeutic to
write a memoir?

00:02:05.033 --> 00:02:08.400
-It is terrifying,
because you're outing people.

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:10.667
And I wanted to call people
by their names,

00:02:10.667 --> 00:02:12.934
because I just want to say,

00:02:12.934 --> 00:02:14.767
"Look what you did to me
when I was 6 years old."

00:02:14.767 --> 00:02:15.801
But I couldn't do it
because, you know,

00:02:15.801 --> 00:02:16.901
I don't want to be sued.

00:02:16.901 --> 00:02:18.667
-Yeah, of course.
-You know, so...

00:02:18.667 --> 00:02:20.901
-Yeah, so you had to change
some of the names, yeah.

00:02:20.901 --> 00:02:22.501
-But it is incredibly cathartic,

00:02:22.501 --> 00:02:25.067
especially because
I wrote it during the pandemic.

00:02:25.067 --> 00:02:27.000
So I was like...

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:29.200
-Yeah. Yeah, exactly.

00:02:29.200 --> 00:02:31.434
And you got it all out.
-I left it all on the floor.

00:02:31.434 --> 00:02:33.868
-But what a great story.
-Yes.

00:02:33.868 --> 00:02:36.434
-And it starts with --
But look at how --

00:02:36.434 --> 00:02:37.934
Look at this cute little girl.

00:02:37.934 --> 00:02:39.501
[ Audience "Awws" ]
I mean, come on.

00:02:39.501 --> 00:02:40.634
Look at what she's done.

00:02:40.634 --> 00:02:42.968
Now, you start like
a little kid,

00:02:42.968 --> 00:02:44.667
and now here you are
"The Woman King."

00:02:44.667 --> 00:02:48.801
Here you go.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:48.801 --> 00:02:51.300
Big deal.
-It is a big deal.

00:02:51.300 --> 00:02:52.534
-This is a big movie.

00:02:52.534 --> 00:02:53.734
Everyone is saying
this is the event movie

00:02:53.734 --> 00:02:55.000
we've been
waiting for now, right?

00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:57.634
-It's the event movie.
Let me tell you something.

00:02:57.634 --> 00:03:01.133
I was 56 when I trained to be
this warrior, now.

00:03:01.133 --> 00:03:02.801
Five hours a day.

00:03:02.801 --> 00:03:04.634
Hour and a half
of weight training,

00:03:04.634 --> 00:03:07.234
three and a half hours
of martial arts,

00:03:07.234 --> 00:03:10.734
punching, 10.0 on the treadmill.

00:03:10.734 --> 00:03:11.801
This is the god complex.

00:03:11.801 --> 00:03:13.601
-Wow!
That's what I'm talking about!

00:03:13.601 --> 00:03:14.934
10.0.

00:03:14.934 --> 00:03:18.234
-And as I was running on that
treadmill, Jimmy, I said,

00:03:18.234 --> 00:03:19.734
"I'm gonna have
a damn heart attack."

00:03:19.734 --> 00:03:21.000
-No, no, no.

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:23.501
Look at how good you look,
though, in the movie.

00:03:23.501 --> 00:03:24.767
I mean, come on. Look at this.

00:03:24.767 --> 00:03:28.634
Look at that.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:28.634 --> 00:03:32.367
That one shot of you flying
in the air with the machete --

00:03:32.367 --> 00:03:33.901
it's just iconic.

00:03:33.901 --> 00:03:36.167
-Listen, if you ever need --

00:03:36.167 --> 00:03:37.868
You know,
anybody ever bothers you,

00:03:37.868 --> 00:03:39.100
I mean, I can take care of it.

00:03:39.100 --> 00:03:40.100
-Yeah, Viola Davis,

00:03:40.100 --> 00:03:41.667
I'll call you first.

00:03:41.667 --> 00:03:43.033
But you've got to be
proud of that.

00:03:43.033 --> 00:03:45.467
That's an iconic scene already,
before the movie is out.

00:03:45.467 --> 00:03:47.234
I go, "Oh, yeah,
for the rest of your life."

00:03:47.234 --> 00:03:49.334
And then I was
talking to you backstage.

00:03:49.334 --> 00:03:51.968
You said it took you
seven years to make this?

00:03:51.968 --> 00:03:53.734
-Seven years.
-Wow.

00:03:53.734 --> 00:03:55.467
-Just fought for seven --
But you know what?

00:03:55.467 --> 00:03:58.234
It takes long to make
any movie in Hollywood.

00:03:58.234 --> 00:03:59.767
-True.
-It really, really does.

00:03:59.767 --> 00:04:02.033
You're fighting for everything.
You're fighting for the actors.

00:04:02.033 --> 00:04:04.100
You're fighting --
And then, when you're finally

00:04:04.100 --> 00:04:06.534
on that soil --
Because we shot in South Africa.

00:04:06.534 --> 00:04:07.634
-I mean, come on.

00:04:07.634 --> 00:04:10.868
-And there is nothing --

00:04:10.868 --> 00:04:13.634
And the girls, the women
in the audience knows,

00:04:13.634 --> 00:04:19.067
there is nothing like looking at
a 250-pound man with a machete

00:04:19.067 --> 00:04:23.033
coming at you, and you know
that, in two seconds or less,

00:04:23.033 --> 00:04:24.534
you're gonna
have to defend yourself.

00:04:24.534 --> 00:04:25.968
-Yeah, yeah.

00:04:25.968 --> 00:04:28.667
-And the only thing I could
think -- I was like, "Pssss!"

00:04:28.667 --> 00:04:29.701
-What are you talking about?

00:04:29.701 --> 00:04:31.868
-I mean, it's terrifying.

00:04:31.868 --> 00:04:34.267
And then they yell "action,"
and that's it.

00:04:34.267 --> 00:04:36.033
-Yeah.
-You are on that man.

00:04:36.033 --> 00:04:39.734
You have your sword, he has his,
and you've got to do it.

00:04:39.734 --> 00:04:41.133
You've got to
take care of yourself.

00:04:41.133 --> 00:04:42.968
-You are a badass in this movie.

00:04:42.968 --> 00:04:45.234
It is unbelievable.
-Mm-hmm.

00:04:45.234 --> 00:04:47.167
-It is iconic.

00:04:47.167 --> 00:04:49.467
Right now, it is at 100%
on Rotten Tomatoes.

00:04:49.467 --> 00:04:51.400
100% fresh.
So congratulations on that.

00:04:51.400 --> 00:04:52.968
Great reviews.
But, I mean, this is --

00:04:52.968 --> 00:04:55.000
-But you've got see it, because
let me tell you something.

00:04:55.000 --> 00:04:57.267
Now, you can attest to it.
-Yeah.

00:04:57.267 --> 00:05:01.400
-From the very moment the
movie opens, you are on a ride.

00:05:01.400 --> 00:05:04.634
-Yes.
-It is a movie for everybody.

00:05:04.634 --> 00:05:06.667
-Yeah, people screaming.
-And, I mean --

00:05:06.667 --> 00:05:08.167
-Was it the
Toronto Film Festival?

00:05:08.167 --> 00:05:11.033
-Toronto Film Festival.
My daughter saw it.

00:05:11.033 --> 00:05:12.701
And my daughter was crying.

00:05:12.701 --> 00:05:16.501
This was, you know,
after the god complex, you know.

00:05:16.501 --> 00:05:17.701
-She's like, "Yeah, it doesn't
help your god complex."

00:05:17.701 --> 00:05:20.834
-My daughter is at her
eye-rolling stage, okay?

00:05:20.834 --> 00:05:22.901
She's like --
I mean, even when she said,

00:05:22.901 --> 00:05:27.100
"Mom, you got a god complex,"
I said, "Oh, my God, Genesis.

00:05:27.100 --> 00:05:28.767
I do not have a god complex."

00:05:28.767 --> 00:05:33.234
She was like,
"Alexa, define god complex."

00:05:35.634 --> 00:05:37.367
And then, after I heard it,
I was like, "Oh, my God.

00:05:37.367 --> 00:05:38.501
I have a god complex."

00:05:38.501 --> 00:05:40.567
-Yeah,
I actually have one, yeah.

00:05:40.567 --> 00:05:42.901
-But, you know,
after the movie, she said,

00:05:42.901 --> 00:05:44.467
"Mommy, I'm so proud of you."

00:05:44.467 --> 00:05:45.634
[ Audience "Awws" ]

00:05:45.634 --> 00:05:48.167
-But they said
the applause was so crazy

00:05:48.167 --> 00:05:50.434
for the first minute
in the movie.

00:05:50.434 --> 00:05:53.467
Once you came on the screen,
everyone went nuts.

00:05:53.467 --> 00:05:55.667
And it was like -- That must
have been exciting, right?

00:05:55.667 --> 00:05:58.367
-That must -- I'm telling you --

00:05:58.367 --> 00:06:01.100
And, first of all,
I mean, I know I say it,

00:06:01.100 --> 00:06:04.767
but there is nothing
that can be said about

00:06:04.767 --> 00:06:08.400
being 56 and running at 10.0
on the treadmill.

00:06:08.400 --> 00:06:11.067
And, I mean,
literally every day was like...

00:06:11.067 --> 00:06:13.167
[ Breathing deeply ]

00:06:13.167 --> 00:06:16.167
-But it's worth it.
You don't see that.

00:06:16.167 --> 00:06:19.868
-To see it on the screen,
I'm like, "I did that."

00:06:19.868 --> 00:06:21.367
-Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:22.968 --> 00:06:24.467
And it will live forever.

00:06:24.467 --> 00:06:25.667
-Yes.
-Congratulations.

00:06:25.667 --> 00:06:26.868
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:06:26.868 --> 00:06:28.901
Here's Viola Davis in
"The Woman King."

00:06:28.901 --> 00:06:30.300
Take a look at this.

00:06:30.300 --> 00:06:33.167
[ Drums playing, chanting ]

00:06:33.167 --> 00:06:37.133
-When the wind blows,
our ancestors push us

00:06:37.133 --> 00:06:41.334
to march into battle
against those who enslave us.

00:06:41.334 --> 00:06:42.434
[ All shouting ]

00:06:42.434 --> 00:06:46.267
When it thunders,
our ancestors demand

00:06:46.267 --> 00:06:49.634
we rip the shackles of doubt
from our minds

00:06:49.634 --> 00:06:52.868
and fight with courage.

00:06:52.868 --> 00:06:56.667
We fight not just for today,
but for the future.

00:06:56.667 --> 00:07:02.200
We are the spear of victory.

00:07:02.200 --> 00:07:05.133
We are the blade of freedom.

00:07:05.133 --> 00:07:07.133
[ All chanting ]

00:07:14.434 --> 00:07:17.200
-Yes!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:17.200 --> 00:07:18.501
Come on!

00:07:18.501 --> 00:07:20.434
Yes!

00:07:20.434 --> 00:07:22.234
Do you feel it?!

00:07:22.234 --> 00:07:23.734
Viola Davis, everybody!

00:07:23.734 --> 00:07:27.601
"The Woman King" opens in
theaters this Friday.

00:07:27.601 --> 00:07:30.133
Karamo joins us after the break.
Stick around, everybody.

